    "reading-passage": {
      "nodeId": "542:3313",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "📖 Reading Passage",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "📖 Reading Passage"
        },
        {
          "text": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Library",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Level: B1 · Topic: The Library"
        },
        {
          "text": "An Afternoon at the Library\n\nI visit the public library near my home at least twice a week. It is a quiet, welcoming place where I can study, read, and borrow books for free.\n\nThe library has two floors. The ground floor has the main hall with rows of bookshelves organised by category: fiction, non-fiction, science, history, and children's books. Each shelf has labels so you can find what you need quickly. There is also a catalogue computer where you can search for a book by title, author, or subject.\n\nAt the reception desk, the librarian helps visitors find books, renew loans, and pay small fines for overdue items. You need a library card to borrow books — up to five at a time, for three weeks.\n\nThe first floor has a reading room with long tables, comfortable chairs, and good lighting. Many students come here to study for exams. There is a 'Quiet Zone' sign, so everyone speaks in a whisper or stays silent.\n\nIn the corner, there is a reference section with encyclopedias, atlases, and academic journals that you can read but not take home. The library also has a small computer area with free internet access and a printer.\n\nEvery Saturday, the library organises a story time for young children and a book club meeting for adults. There is a noticeboard near the entrance with information about upcoming events.\n\nI love the library because it offers so much more than just books — it's a community space for learning and discovery.",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "An Afternoon at the Library I visit the public library near my home at least twice a week. It is a quiet, welcoming place where I can study, read, and borrow books for free. The library has two floors. The ground floor has the main hall with rows of bookshelves organised by category: fiction, non-fiction, science, history, and children's books. Each shelf has labels so you can find what you need quickly. There is also a catalogue computer where you can search for a book by title, author, or subject. At the reception desk, the librarian helps visitors find books, renew loans, and pay small fines for overdue items. You need a library card to borrow books — up to five at a time, for three weeks. The first floor has a reading room with long tables, comfortable chairs, and good lighting. Many students come here to study for exams. There is a 'Quiet Zone' sign, so everyone speaks in a whisper or stays silent. In the corner, there is a reference section with encyclopedias, atlases, and academic journals that you can read but not take home. The library also has a small computer area with free internet access and a printer. Every Saturday, the library organises a story time for young children and a book club meeting for adults. There is a noticeboard near the entrance with information about upcoming events. I love the library because it offers so much more than just books — it's a community space for learning and discovery."
        },
        {
          "text": "Comprehension Questions",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "Comprehension Questions"
        },
        {
          "text": "1. How often does the writer visit the library?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "1. How often does the writer visit the library?"
        },
        {
          "text": "2. How are the bookshelves organised?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "2. How are the bookshelves organised?"
        },
        {
          "text": "3. What do you need to borrow books?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "3. What do you need to borrow books?"
        },
        {
          "text": "4. What rule applies in the reading room?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "4. What rule applies in the reading room?"
        },
        {
          "text": "5. What events does the library organise on Saturdays?",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "5. What events does the library organise on Saturdays?"
        }
      ]
    },
    "idioms-phrases": {
      "nodeId": "542:3326",
      "lines": [
        {
          "text": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases",
          "depth": 1,
          "name": "💬 Idioms, Phrasal Verbs & Key Phrases"
        },
        {
          "text": "by the book",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "by the book"
        },
        {
          "text": "following rules exactly",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "following rules exactly"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The librarian does everything by the book — no exceptions.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"The librarian does everything by the book — no exceptions.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "an open book",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "an open book"
        },
        {
          "text": "a person with no secrets, easy to understand",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "a person with no secrets, easy to understand"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"He's an open book — you always know what he's thinking.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"He's an open book — you always know what he's thinking.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "take out (a book)",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "take out (a book)"
        },
        {
          "text": "borrow from the library",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "borrow from the library"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"I took out three novels last week.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"I took out three novels last week.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "look up",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "look up"
        },
        {
          "text": "search for information",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "search for information"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Can you look up the author's name in the catalogue?\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"Can you look up the author's name in the catalogue?\""
        },
        {
          "text": "check out",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "check out"
        },
        {
          "text": "borrow an item; also: examine something",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "borrow an item; also: examine something"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"I checked out a history book from the library.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"I checked out a history book from the library.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "be on the same page",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "be on the same page"
        },
        {
          "text": "agree or have the same understanding",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "agree or have the same understanding"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"Let's make sure we're on the same page before the meeting.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"Let's make sure we're on the same page before the meeting.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "read between the lines",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "read between the lines"
        },
        {
          "text": "understand the hidden meaning",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "understand the hidden meaning"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"She didn't say no, but if you read between the lines, she's not interested.\"",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "\"She didn't say no, but if you read between the lines, she's not interested.\""
        },
        {
          "text": "turn over a new leaf",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "turn over a new leaf"
        },
        {
          "text": "start behaving in a better way",
          "depth": 2,
          "name": "start behaving in a better way"
        },
        {
          "text": "\"He turned over a new leaf and started studying at the library every day.\"",
          "depth": 2,
